WMA decoders for core B, from Rockbox (https://github.com/Rockbox/rockbox, master at
f2eaa15ac2cb0fe97b58d9c69e43777f9eb94cb4, fetched 2026-10-15):

  libwma    lib/rbcodec/codecs/libwma     WMA v1/v2 (0x160/0x161), fixed point
  pro/      lib/rbcodec/codecs/libwmapro  WMA Pro (0x162), fixed point, mono/stereo
  shared    lib/rbcodec/codecs/lib        mdct.c, fft-ffmpeg.c, mdct_lookup.c,
                                          ffmpeg_bitstream.c and their headers
and WMA Lossless (0x163) from FFmpeg (below).

Both are ports of FFmpeg's decoders (wmadec.c by the FFmpeg project, wmaprodec.c by
Baptiste Coudurier, Benjamin Larsson, Ulion, Sascha Sommer), LGPL-2.1-or-later as the
file headers say; Rockbox's own files (wmafixed.*, codeclib glue) are GPL-2.0-or-later.
Both are compatible with ReChord's GPL-3.0. mdct_lookup.c's tables come from Tremor
(BSD-style, Xiph.Org). Not taken: Rockbox's codec glue (wma.c, wmapro.c), libasf (our
ASF demuxer is firmware/audio/asf.c), libwmavoice, the ARM/ColdFire assembly (ARM-mode
asm; the C paths are used, so core B and the host reference compute alike).

Local changes (each marked "ReChord" in the source):
- codecs.h, codeclib.h, platform.h, wma_wfx.h: our stand-ins for Rockbox's codec API
  headers: empty IRAM attributes, no-op DEBUGF/LOGF, byte swaps on GCC builtins, a
  big-endian 32-bit read as one unaligned load (AV_RB32), av_log2 on CLZ, and the
  asf_waveformatex_t the decoders take (from libasf/asf.h).
- Include paths flattened (<codecs/lib/codeclib.h> -> "codeclib.h", libasf -> wma_wfx.h);
  the per-CPU IRAM tiers in wmadec.h / pro/wmaprodec.h replaced by empty defines;
  WMAPRO_MAX_CHANNELS fixed at 2 (Rockbox: 8 on large-memory targets).
- wmafixed.c/h: long -> int32_t/uint32_t in fsincos, fixsqrt32 (a 64-bit host long
  changed the CORDIC's arithmetic).
- wmadata.h: noisetable_exp is const (32 KiB in code RAM rather than .data); LSP mode
  reads it doubled (NOISE() in wmadeci.c) instead of doubling the table in place.
- wmadeci.c: scratch_buf typed fixed32; frame_out_buf cleared in wma_decode_init (it is
  static: a previous track's overlap leaked into the next track's first frame).
- pro/wmaprodec.c: the output buffers cleared in decode_init, for the same reason.
- ffmpeg_bitstream.c: the VLC code sort is a Shell sort on the code (qsort's comparator
  took an int difference of two 31-bit keys, which can overflow); same order, no libc.

lossless/wmalldec.c: FFmpeg n7.1 libavcodec/wmalosslessdec.c (Baptiste Coudurier,
Benjamin Larsson, Ulion, Sascha Sommer, Andreas Oman, Mashiat Sarker Shakkhar;
LGPL-2.1-or-later), with the C lossless_audiodsp routines, made standalone (marked
"ReChord"): wmall_init()/wmall_decode() instead of the AVCodec callbacks, the frame
and sample buffers from the caller's allocator sized to the stream (FFmpeg: fixed
16384-sample arrays), Rockbox's bit reader/writer, mono/stereo only, the decode loop
of FFmpeg's decode.c (a packet is fed again from where the last call stopped; the
end of the stream is drained) in firmware/coreb/b_wmall.c. Bit exact against ffmpeg
on whole files (16 and 24 bit); on a cut file the last frame, read past the data,
may differ (both decoders then read what follows in their buffers).
2026-10-18 (docs/HIFI_PLAN.md): lms_update zeroes only the part of lms_updates that can be
nonzero (FFmpeg clears up to 1 KiB after every sample of every filter: 29 % / 50 % of 16- /
24-bit files' core-B time), and the LMS dot products run 4 taps a turn, skipping the update
when the residue is 0. The same array contents and sums: still bit exact.

Output scale (firmware/coreb/b_wma.c, b_wmapro.c, b_wmall.c): libwma gives 2.29 fixed point
(Rockbox sample depth 29) with inverted polarity, libwmapro 2.25 (depth 25); both are
clipped to +-1.0 and left-justified in the 32-bit I2S word; WMA Lossless 16-bit
samples << 16, 24-bit << 8. Checked against FFmpeg's
float decoders: 92-105 dB SNR on ffmpeg-encoded WMA v1/v2, 58-86 dB on Windows-encoded
WMA v2 (bit reservoir, block switching), 90-99 dB on WMA Pro (16-96 kHz).
